==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|mutabilis||liable to change}}; {{suffix|mutate|able|lang=en}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[change|Changeable]]; inclined to [[mutate]].
# {{lb|en|programming|of a variable}} Having a value that is changeable during [[program]] [[execution]].
#* '''2011''', David Flanagan, ''JavaScript: The Definitive Guide'':
#*: A value of a '''mutable''' type can change. Objects and arrays are '''mutable''': a JavaScript program can change the values of object properties and array elements. Numbers, booleans, null, and undefined are immutable.

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|immutable}}

